Dubbin</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Shih</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Simon</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Statistical design of reverse dye microarrays</article-title><source>Bioinformatics</source><year>2003</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>803</fpage><lpage>10</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12724289</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>YH</given-names></name><name><surname>Speed</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Design issues for cDNA mciroarray experiments</article-title><source>Nature Reviews Genetics</source><year>2002</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>579</fpage><lpage>588</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12154381</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Forster</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Costa</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Roy</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Cooke</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Maratou</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Triple-target microarray experiments: a novel experimental strategy</article-title><source>BMC Genomics</source><year>2004</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>13</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15018645</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Staal</surname><given-names>YCM</given-names></name><name><surname>van Herwijnen</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>van Schooten</surname><given-names>FJ</given-names></name><name><surname>van Delft</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Applicat